From 046bc51debb1c34d09894b369eb3c2face5b5388 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon <jon@pionex.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:55:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] drm/imagination: promote BXM-4-64 revision 36.56.104.183
 to supported

The A733's BXM-4-64 MC1 (BVNC 36.56.104.183) has now been validated on
hardware: <Vulkan CTS version> passes on <board>, with firmware
powervr/rogue_36.56.104.183_v1.fw (1.1.OS@6976702) and Mesa's pvr driver,
which already carries this GPU ID (0x36104183).

Move the case from PVR_GPU_EXPERIMENTAL to PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED, so the driver
binds without requiring the exp_hw_support module parameter, matching the
36.52.104.182 precedent.

NOTE: do not send until the line above is filled in with a real result.

Signed-off-by: Jon <jon@pionex.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
index 6be7fc9..05c2c81 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imagination/pvr_device.c
@@ -533,10 +533,8 @@ pvr_gpu_support_level(const struct pvr_gpu_id *gpu_id)
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(33, 15, 11, 3):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 52, 104, 182):
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 53, 104, 796):
-		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;
-
 	case PVR_PACKED_BVNC(36, 56, 104, 183):
-		return PVR_GPU_EXPERIMENTAL;
+		return PVR_GPU_SUPPORTED;
 
 	default:
 		return PVR_GPU_UNKNOWN;
-- 
